    "multi_column_kTT6qT": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "text_block_w6maqT": {
          "type": "text_block",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/215417-690x460-shape-symmetry.jpg",
            "title": "DIAMOND SYMMETRY",
            "text": "<p>Symmetry refers to the quality of the diamond facets in terms of their proportion and alignment. Diamonds with a high-quality cut typically also exhibit excellent symmetry, making these two attributes closely related. You can find the symmetry grade listed on the IGI or GIA certificate.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "text_block_ABaPrw": {
          "type": "text_block",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Flourescence_df1dd4e4-47b7-424e-b62c-f95394eca00f.png",
            "title": "DIAMOND FLUORESCENCE",
            "text": "<p>Diamond fluorescence describes how a diamond reacts to ultraviolet (UV) light. This reaction is graded based on the diamond's response to long-wave UV, which is present in daylight. While fluorescence can make diamonds appear blue or yellow under UV light, it generally doesn't change their appearance under normal lighting conditions or compromise the diamond's structural integrity.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "text_block_jR8dxD": {
          "type": "text_block",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/GIA_Cert.jpg",
            "title": "DIAMOND CERTIFICATION",
            "text": "<p>Diamonds are evaluated using a grading scale established by the Gemological Institute of America (GIA), which considers cut, color, clarity, and carat weight. These four factors, known as the 4 C's, are widely recognized as the standard criteria for assessing and determining the quality of diamonds.</p><p>Milano offers diamonds certified by GIA, EGL USA and IGI</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      },
